  "selected": [
    {
      "id": "cmip6-mlotst-definition",
      "severity": "must",
      "path": "concepts/cmip6-mlotst-definition.md",
      "sha256": "7c9f821afb300a640b26dbd03993d309a09793518640191dc82d641f6a4f5cb5",
      "reason": "The operator must use the published mlotst sigma-t/buoyancy criterion (ΔB = 0.0003 m s-2, ≈ Δρ 0.03 kg m-3 at local pressure) and recognize that mlotst is computed online every time step and then monthly averaged.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Pass `ref_depth` = the model's shallowest level to `compute_mixed_layer_depth` (mlotst is referenced to the ocean surface, not 10 m); the result comes close to `mlotst` but never identical.",
        "Expect operator MLD from monthly-mean `thetao`/`so` to be shallower than `mlotst`; state the three causes — reference level, displaced-parcel density at local pressure vs σ0 difference, and averaging instantaneous MLDs vs MLD of averaged profiles — as definitional, not model error; exclude columns where the threshold is never reached."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "monthly-means-are-time-averages",
      "severity": "must",
      "path": "pitfalls/monthly-means-are-time-averages.md",
      "sha256": "df6b5c23460f88f1522e5c6a665e1efbb8322c3ae876c885530f3019aa284ee0",
      "reason": "MLD is nonlinear, so computing it offline from monthly-mean thetao and so cannot match the monthly mean of the online diagnostic, which is the key reason exact agreement is not expected.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "MLD is nonlinear: compute the MLD of each monthly profile then average, never average T/S first (that MLD is systematically shallower); state which order was used.",
        "The March/September climatology is the plain mean of that month's 30 values over the years (no day weights); sub-monthly variance is not recoverable."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "common-comparison-mask",
      "severity": "must",
      "path": "methods/common-comparison-mask.md",
      "sha256": "bbb98200f52b4a692ce097704b8c438179a795a44bec6b856c03cf31931af4ea",
      "reason": "The comparison, ranking and coverage percentages must be built on a common mask of cells where both operator MLD and mlotst are defined, applied consistently to both fields.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Build one shared mask over both fields per model/month with `build_comparison_mask` and apply with `.where(mask)` before any metric; report its cell counts and the ocean-area fraction.",
        "Take bias/RMSE from the shared sample (the `mean_data`, `mean_reference` that `compute_difference_metrics` returns), not means computed over different cells."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "missing-values-and-land-cells",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "pitfalls/missing-values-and-land-cells.md",
      "sha256": "f576244f13dde06fed1777eaa9721c68844f61758f66fac704b44f1551e90df2",
      "reason": "CMIP6 land and below-sea-floor cells are marked with 1e20 and must be CF-masked before computing MLD or area statistics so they do not dominate sums and means.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Read with xarray so 1e20 decodes to NaN (a value near 1e20 or 9.97e36 in output is an unmasked fill); use NaN-aware reductions with weights masked to the same cells.",
        "Build each field's valid mask from the field itself: `thetao` and `so` masks can differ within the same model and month."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "omip-native-grid-vs-regridded",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "methods/omip-native-grid-vs-regridded.md",
      "sha256": "8ff046ffbadc5794fcd2f8fe93d3bb947c736dec650aa3a3cd6e2412b7da8e68",
      "reason": "The MLD comparison and masks should be computed on each model’s native grid and regridded only for the Figure 1 maps and pattern displays, since regridding changes the land-sea mask and breaks conservation.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Regrid only for the Figure 1 maps/cell-by-cell comparison; use method 'conservative' going to a coarser grid and state the method used.",
        "Keep area means and counts on each model's own grid with its own `areacello`; a regridded RMSE/correlation depends on the method."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "omip-weighted-means-and-integrals",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "methods/omip-weighted-means-and-integrals.md",
      "sha256": "89de52676ae54db8f5897bc77a08c78de3f776696db0020935a38b790c302cbe",
      "reason": "Surface MLD means and area fractions should be area-weighted over all ocean cells using the model’s own cell areas rather than treated as unweighted cell averages.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "All map statistics must be area-weighted with `areacello`: `compute_difference_metrics` weights by area by default, and `analyze_correlation` needs `weighting='area'` for the pattern correlation.",
        "The >20 m exceedance is a share of area, not of cells, with missing cells out of the denominator — use `compute_exceedance_fraction`, which also returns the area behind the percentage."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "cmip6-thetao-potential-temperature",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "concepts/cmip6-thetao-potential-temperature.md",
      "sha256": "cf8b1424a04be2e18362300d2e76d09e3f958f9d6a451c733a0cf9938968e73c",
      "reason": "thetao is potential temperature referenced to 0 dbar, so it equals in-situ temperature only at the surface and density below the surface must account for this.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "`thetao` is potential temperature; no `bigthetao` exists for these models, so any TEOS-10 density calculation must use the potential-temperature route (`temperature_kind()` reads this from metadata)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "cmip6-so-practical-salinity",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "concepts/cmip6-so-practical-salinity.md",
      "sha256": "96f2763290996040d675ca6e8f997ea29fa320b8f6e6793bf2c6fcb739345e19",
      "reason": "so is Practical Salinity, so density calculations using TEOS-10 require deriving Absolute Salinity rather than treating the stored values as Absolute Salinity.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "`so` is practical salinity (units string \"0.001\", values of order 35): difference it against practical-salinity observations directly, but convert S_P to S_A before calling gsw routines that expect Absolute Salinity."
      ]
    }
